  "id": "tonic-activation",
  "term": "tonic activation",
  "definition": "Tonic activation is a sustained increase in neural activity that persists across task performance, rather than appearing only at brief event moments. In this context, it refers to ongoing activation seen in particular brain regions during an incentive condition.",
